# project: copied from validation/python/lint/.semgrepignore. Copy to the root of the scanned project and run semgrep with `--project-root .` there.
# Semgrep reads `.semgrepignore` only at its project root; without one it applies its
# built-in default list, which skips every folder named "test"/"tests" and so would
# silently exclude the project's own tests (and the test-scoped `kit.tests.*` rules).
# List every exclusion explicitly and never add a tests/test pattern here.

.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
htmlcov/
coverage/
# The kit's own deliberate violation fixtures, when the kit is vendored into the project.
**/semgrep/fixtures/

# project: the validation kit lives at the repo root, outside backend/; nothing else to exclude.
